  "_note_reactions": "A `reaction` block is what makes a reaction-cost spell reach the board at all: combat.gd fires the named trigger at the moment it happens and resolves the answer itself, so a reaction is never a button (combat-design.md §2 — zero prompts). `counter` means the trigger's spell unravels on a failed save; `min_level` is how low the reaction stoops, so a 3rd-level slot is not spent to swat a cantrip. Counterspell's numbers come from its catalog description: a Constitution save at DC 10 + the countered spell's level, and a countered caster keeps the slot — the action is the whole cost.",
  "counterspell": {
    "cost": "reaction", "shape": "single", "range_ft": 60, "save": "con",
    "reaction": {"trigger": "spell_cast", "counter": true, "min_level": 1}
  },
  "_note_zones": "2026-09-16: `zone: true` on an area spell keeps it on its hexes (combat.gd zones) instead of resolving once against whoever stood there: a buff zone (Darkness, Fog Cloud) dresses and undresses occupants as they come and go, a save/damage zone (Web, Spirit Guardians, Wall of Fire) rolls against a creature the turn it starts inside or steps in, once per turn. Concentration zones end with the caster's concentration; emanations walk with the caster.",
  "_note_buffs": "2026-09-16: `buff` is a status the target wears (combat.gd _apply_buff): ac, bonus_to_hit, bonus_save, bonus_damage, resist / resist_random, extra_action, speed_mult, no_attack, condition (+sticky), and an `effects` dict of conditions.json-style adv/dis. shape self = the caster, allies = everyone on the caster's side within range_ft, single = one ally (or the enemy who fails the save when the spell has one). `rounds` is its life without concentration. Dice bonuses are their averages (Bless 1d4 -> 2). `conditions: []` blanks the regex draft's guess. Marked non_combat: nothing on this board models what they do.",
